Directory "no-such-dir" does not exist.

Usage:
    find-covers [options] <inputDir> <outputDir>

    inputDir      the tree whose audio files are looked at; only read.
    outputDir     where a copy of each file a cover was found for is written,
                  at the same relative path, with the cover embedded. Created
                  if missing, and refused if it lies inside inputDir.
Options:
    -h, --help      Print this help page.
    -i, --ignore-folder-covers
                    Also look for a file whose folder holds a cover image
                    (folder.jpg, cover.png, an image sharing its name, ...),
                    rather than taking that image as its cover.
    -m, --min-megapixels <megapixels>
                    A cover smaller than this - embedded, or the image
                    beside the file - is looked to be replaced, and only by
                    one with more pixels. A fraction is allowed; 0 keeps
                    every cover. Default 0.25
    -n, --dry-run   Only list the files that would be looked for; nothing is
                    searched or written.
    -A, --ai        Let language models help (docs/models.md). Without -A no
                    step asks one; the commands this one starts are handed it.
    -v, --verbose   Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                    failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                    lines.
    -q, --quiet     Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
    -x, --set <name=value>
                    Override a setting for this run, over the settings file;
                    repeatable. A secret is refused - the settings file is where
                    it goes. The settings page lists the names.
